Information on all output files from the program:

GloveData.csv: raw data pipelined directly from arduino board sensor readings. Columns are labeled. This file is
functionally useless.

PositionData_Continuous.csv: From inside the program, you may decide to record live position data. In that case,
it is stored in this file. There are 35 total columns: real-time timestamp, runtime timestamp, all quanterion positions
at that time, all flex sensor data at that time

PositionData_Snapshots.csv: From inside the program, you may decide to take snapshots of live position data.
In that case, it is stored in this file. There are 36 total columns: real-time timestamp, runtime timestamp, all
quanterion positions at that time, all flex sensor data at that time, and the flag of the position you selected. If you
click 'Snapshots under the second dropdown menu,' you are presented with 5 position options. To write a sample to a file,
simply orient your hand in the corresponding position and click the position you are in (i.e. thumbs down).
To re-train your basic position identification model, move this file to position_Identification and run
train_hand_pose_model.py.

(Note, V is a placeholder for mid, pink, point, ring, thumb, or 2) (2 is the wrist gyroscope)
Gyro_log_V.csv: These are created when you attempt to collect data on your gyro sensor error. To do this,
 move your glove to a zero position, click 'record gyro', then move your hand around a bit. Finally, return your hand
 to your starting position and click 'stop gyro recording.' This creates a sample error for the gyroscope given
 some tracked gyroscope data. This file is used in Python\gyro_calibration, and the contents are copied to data/raw/gryo_log.csv
 (within the Python\gyro_calibration directory). Note that you will want to copy Gyro_log_V_s.csv into data/raw/gryo_stationary.csv
 at the same time. Further implementation details can be found in Python\gyro_calibration\info

Gyro_log_V_s.csv: Created alongside Gyro_log_V.csv. You will have to uncomment the secondary 'FILE_MAP' variable assignment
inside of SensorDataProcessor.py, GyroRecorder class to create these files. The intent is that you will keep your hand
motionless for these recordings to capture raw sensor drift.
